  <page_number>51</page_number>
  <running_head>LYRICA.</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <signature>D 2</signature>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <p cont="true"><l>Pacis dulcia Candida</l><l>Plebi restituat otia subdita.</l></p>
    <p><l>Audax Guisiadum genus</l><l>Deceptum magicis cantibus, &amp; sibi</l><l>Francum debita somnians</l><l>Regna, &amp; pollicitis excitum fbericis</l><l>Terra misfcuit æthera.</l><l>Produxit q, suis seditionibus</l><l>Belli iurgia ciuici,</l><l>Et Gallos variis cladibus obruit.</l></p>
    <p><l>Audax Gens Lotharingica</l><l>Dumse Pontificum relligionibus</l><l>Addictam magis omnibus</l><l>Fingit, dum veteres, quas vocat, hæreses</l><l>Ardet perdere funditus,</l><l>O quàm multiplices cauta reconditis</l><l>Texit pectoribus dolos,</l><l>Fraudes, insidias, perfidiam &amp; scelus,</l><l>Regi perniciem suo,</l><l>Gallis seruitium turpius apparans.</l></p>
    <p><l>Sed qui sceptra Deus tibi,</l><l>Rex Henrice, dedit Gallica flectere,</l><l>Hic mentis quoque prouidæ</l><l>Iunctum Consilium viribus addidit.</l><l>Sic nunc lethiferam caues</l><l>Gentis perfidiam fortior impiæ.</l><l>Sic regnum tibi traditum</l><l>Iamiam propitio Numine vindicas.</l></p>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Printed page numeral "51" at top right; running head "LYRICA." centred. Some words in the verse are uncertain in the scan (e.g. "fbericis", "Iamiam", "Numine"); the bracketed q-with-mark in "Produxit q," and the signature "D 2" are as seen. Ornamental capitals and the "2" after the signature rendered as printed.</notes>
</page>
